Z||000003||ur2biteme||01-13-2001||06:35 PM||||where'd you get the wheels there?  not bad looking semi-stock looking.  what's the logo on the sail pannel?  nice car there.  <P>now why am i being reminded constantly of "the one that got away" so much these days.  there was an '84 i would have picked up instead of the '87 i have now that looks like your "new" car in the picture.  funny thing was, the original paint looked as good as the paint in the picture there.  'sigh' they had just got that car to the lot and it wouldnt pass emissions.  had to auction it off out of state.<P>------------------<BR>Bob's '87 econo coupe<BR>170k awaiting a tranny:(<BR> <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/ur2biteme" TARGET=_blank>http://members.fortunecity.com/ur2biteme</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Motorhead||01-13-2001||10:09 PM||||My "RED" '86 is A daily driver!!<BR>The '84 doesn't know what it is yet!!<BR>It runs, but doesn't know how or where yet!<BR>The sail panels in the pic of the red car have decals that "SUCK"!<BR>I have a set of panels I got from Paul McKibben that are beautiful! Laser cut "Pegasus" logos.<BR>Also have a set of GT wheels to be re-finished from FieroDave. Along with A "WING" from the same source!<BR>The Formula rear facia is in the shed to be matched up with a F355 nose and ground effects before new "VERY RED" paint.<BR>A "Warmed Over" 2.5 is also on the engine stand. V-8 is going into the '84! Finances and wife allowing!  <IMG SRC="http://pip.pennock.nl/uploads/redfiero.jpg"> <BR>Nose and wheels!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://pip.pennock.nl/uploads/car10.jpg"> <BR>Ground Effects!<BR>Amid all of this an '86 auto is in the works for the wife.  Busy summer. Huh!<BR>Keeps me out of trouble though!<BR><P>------------------<BR> bluewater46@hotmail.com<BR>1986 coupe<BR>1984 coupe<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://content.communities.msn.com/isapi/fetch.dill?action=view_photo&ID_Community=BluewatersPics&1"> ||||reg||1
